---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/icons/Icon.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'April 30, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that cover your use of Chancey: who can use it, acceptable use, payments, disclaimers, and how to reach us."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { name: 'Terms of Service', href: '/terms/' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="container">
    <div class="article">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        <div class="notice">
          <span class="notice-icon" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="lightning" size={22} /></span>
          <div>
            <strong>Working draft</strong>
            These terms are in final legal review for launch. Big changes will show up in the app
            and at the top of this page.
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>Agreement</h2>
        <p>
          By using Chancey, you agree to these Terms of Service and the <a href="/privacy/"
            >Privacy Policy</a>. If you don't agree, please don't use Chancey. If you use Chancey
          for an organization, you confirm you have the right to bind that organization.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Eligibility</h2>
        <p>
          You must be at least 18 years old, or the age of majority where you live, whichever is
          greater. You also confirm that lottery play is legal where you live.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What Chancey is</h2>
        <p>
          Chancey is an information and convenience tool for lottery players. It helps you pick
          numbers, save sets, scan tickets, and check published draw results.
        </p>
        <h3>What Chancey is not</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Not a lottery retailer. We cannot sell tickets or pay prizes.</li>
          <li>Not part of any state, provincial, or national lottery.</li>
          <li>
            Not a predictor. Lottery draws are random and Chancey cannot improve the odds of
            winning.
          </li>
          <li>Not a substitute for the lottery's results or claims process.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your account and acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          You are responsible for keeping your account secure and for what happens through it.
          Don't:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use Chancey if you are under 18 or the local age of majority.</li>
          <li>Try to break, scrape, or reverse engineer the service.</li>
          <li>Upload images of other people's documents, IDs, or sensitive personal data.</li>
          <li>Use Chancey to run, advertise, or recruit for any unlawful gambling activity.</li>
          <li>Use Chancey to harass, abuse, defraud, or impersonate anyone.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Subscriptions and payments</h2>
        <p>
          The core experience is free today. If we offer paid features, we will show the price,
          billing schedule, and how to cancel before you buy. Payments run through the platform or
          checkout you used to subscribe (web checkout, App Store, or Google Play). To cancel, use
          the same channel.
        </p>
        <p>
          Refunds follow the policy of the platform that processed your payment, plus any consumer
          rights you have where you live that we can't waive.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your responsibility</h2>
        <p>
          Always check important ticket info and winning status with the official lottery. The
          number tools are for fun and organization. They do not predict or improve odds. Keep the
          original ticket safe — Chancey is a checking tool, not a payout service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          Chancey is provided "as is" with no warranties, to the maximum extent the law allows.
          We do not guarantee the service will run without breaks or errors. Draw matching is
          based on what the lottery posts. The lottery is the source of truth.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Limit of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent the law allows, Chancey is not liable for indirect, incidental,
          consequential, special, or example damages. We are not liable for lost prizes, lost
          profits, or lost data from your use of the service. Some places don't allow these
          limits. In those places, our liability is limited to the smallest amount the law
          allows.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Termination</h2>
        <p>
          You can stop using Chancey any time. We may suspend or close accounts that break these
          terms, that we have to remove by law, or that pose a security risk. If your account is
          closed, your data is handled per the Privacy policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms over time. Big changes will show up in the app and at the top
          of this page, with a new "last updated" date. Continued use after the changes means you
          accept the new terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Governing law and disputes</h2>
        <p>
          The governing law and dispute resolution will be set at launch. For now, please reach
          us through the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> with any concerns. We will work with
          you in good faith.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms? Send a message through the <a href="/contact/">contact
            form</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
